  "text": "File No.P.39012/5/2018-L&R Government of India Ministry of Commerce and Industry Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (L&R Section) Udyog Bhawan, New Delhi Dated the 7th July, 2025 OFFICE MEMORANDUM Subject: Pneumatic Tyres and Tubes for Automotive Vehicles (Quality Control) Order, 2009 - Revise list of 766 tyre sizes/types (635+131run flat tyres)- reg. The undersigned is directed to refer to Minutes of IMC Meeting held on 14.05.2025 in hybrid mode (offline/online) to discuss exclusion of Pneumatic Tyres and Tubes from QCO 2009 (Copy Enclosed) and to say that w.r.t Para 8 of said Minutes, it is further stated that as per provisions contained under sub-clause (a) to (f) of Clause 3 of the \"Pneumatic Tyres and Tubes for Automotive (Quality Control) Order, 2009\" (Copy Enclosed), certain categories of Tyres have been exempted from the application of the provisions of the said Quality Control Order, 2009. In pursuance of the Sub-Clause (f) of Clause 3 of said Order, 2009, a Committee was constituted to review the list of Tyres not manufactured domestically and Imported by the Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs) for selling in replacement market through their authorized dealers. 2. The said Committee has reviewed and finalized the lists as under: • Annexure-I: Updated list of 635 tyres sizes (629 existing +30 additions - 24 deletions). • Annexure-11: The list of 131 run-flat tyres with BIS text noted as a footnote, carried forward from the previous list. A Copy of the list of Tyres can also be obtained from the website of this Department https://dipp.gov.in. 3. This issue with the approval of the Competent Authority. Encl: as above n G (0 - ~G\\ v-,----5:--- ~ ~ ) :....------- A '\"\"\\ _ 0 \\ ' 0 \\' (Rajesh Rawat) Under Secretary to the Govt. of India e.mail: rajesh.rawat@nic.in -- 1 of 28 -- To 1. Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs(CBIC) (Kind Attention: Shri Anupam Prakash, Joint Secretary (Customs), Department of Revenue, 